CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "2c3c43fe-7cff-4324-ad4f-4318aae71ef6",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-22T01:22:22Z",
  "ticket_id": "e471-dda3",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "When /dso:brainstorm reaches the end of its Phase 1 understanding loop, a dso:confluence-researcher sub-agent is dispatched with the accumulated feature understanding as context; it derives CQL keywords automatically, searches all accessible Confluence spaces, and returns the top 5 most relevant page summaries ranked by Confluence's native CQL relevance score (configurable via `confluence.max_results` in dso-config.conf) \u2014 without the user providing any URLs.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability where the brainstorm agent automatically dispatches a researcher sub-agent with specific search and ranking behaviors"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Reference documents (Confluence-authenticated and public URLs) are fetched via `confluence-fetch.sh` and stored in `/tmp/dso-ref-cache/` with a 1-hour mtime-based TTL and 0600 file permissions; repeated calls within the cache window serve content from disk and emit a `[cache hit: <url>]` message to stderr without making any network request; concurrent writes to the same cache file are serialized via `flock`.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior of how reference documents are fetched, cached, and served with specific technical properties"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When CONFLUENCE_EMAIL or CONFLUENCE_API_TOKEN environment variables are not configured, Confluence-authenticated URLs are skipped with a stderr warning and all other workflow steps continue uninterrupted. Credentials MUST be sourced from environment variables ONLY; credential detection at startup rejects credentials found in dso-config.conf with a security warning.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior for credential handling and error recovery that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When `confluence.roadmap_research_enabled=true` in dso-config.conf, /dso:roadmap dispatches dso:confluence-researcher at the start of its exploration phase using the roadmap theme as context; when the flag is absent or false, the step is skipped silently. Default: false (opt-in).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior conditional on a configuration flag, specifying how the system will behave after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When the CQL search returns zero results, the agent emits `[confluence-research: no results for query: <keywords>]`; when Confluence returns HTTP 400 (malformed query), the agent emits `[confluence-research: invalid query: <keywords>, error: 400]`; the session continues in both cases.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior for how the agent handles specific error conditions and continues operation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "confluence-fetch.sh domain guard FAILS CLOSED: unset `confluence.base_url` rejects all Confluence-authenticated URLs; trailing-slash base_url is normalized; tiny-link resolution via `curl --location-trusted=false -L` strips Authorization header on redirect to non-base_url domains. Integration test asserts the domain guard behavior for (i) unset base_url, (ii) trailing slash, (iii) off-base_url redirect during tiny-link resolution.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable security behavior of the domain guard system (rejection, normalization, header stripping) that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "An integration test suite at tests/integration/test-confluence-integration.sh validates using a local HTTP stub fixture on a dynamically-allocated port (no live Confluence required): (a) the researcher returns at least 1 of top 3 summaries containing a keyword from the seed topic; (b) confluence-fetch.sh serves cached content without network requests and emits `[cache hit: <url>]` to stderr for files within the 1-hour TTL; (c) credential-in-dso-config.conf placement triggers a startup rejection; (d) trailing-slash and missing base_url cases produce explicit error messages.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behaviors (caching, validation, error handling) that the system should exhibit after implementation, phrased as ongoing test coverage of expected properties"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "dso-config.conf schema additions documented in CONFIGURATION-REFERENCE.md: `confluence.base_url`, `confluence.max_results`, `confluence.roadmap_research_enabled`, multi-valued `confluence.reference.url` / `confluence.reference.tags` pairs. All keys additive; no changes to existing schema.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "documentation updates describing new config schema additions are one-time tasks, distinct from the durable property of the system supporting those configurations"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
